## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end streaming ingestion, lightweight validation, data quality scoring, and practical cost governance in a beginner-friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams + Lambda ingestion
- Lightweight JSON validation and 0–100 data quality scoring
- Parquet storage in S3 with region/date partitioning
- DLQ handling for invalid records
- DynamoDB for regional budgets and a guard lambda to pause ingestion
- Lifecycle policies for cost control; CloudWatch observability

## Code Example
```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const r of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(r.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString('utf8'));
    const ok = validate(payload);
    if (!ok) {
      await sendToDLQ(payload);
      continue;
    }
    const score = computeQuality(payload);
    await writeParquetToS3(payload, score);
  }
  return { status: 'ok' };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution and optional fields in this pipeline?
- How would you validate and recover from late data while respecting the budget guard?
- What monitoring dashboards would you build to track data quality, cost, and DLQ trends?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a compliant, scalable multi-region telemetry pipeline with per-tenant governance, residency rules, and cost controls using AWS DVA primitives and OpenTelemetry.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant policy management in DynamoDB
- Residency-aware routing to region streams
- Exactly-once processing and idempotent writes
- End-to-end tracing with OpenTelemetry across components
- Data lifecycle: per-tenant retention, purge strategies, and cost controls
- Testing: residency canaries, audit validation, DR scenarios

## Code Example

```typescript
// Pseudo routing function
function routeEvent(evt: TelemetryEvent){
  const policy = getPolicy(evt.tenantId);
  if (policy.residency === 'home' && evt.region !== policy.homeRegion){
    throw new Error('Residency violation');
  }
  const targetStream = policy.replicate ? `${policy.homeRegion}-stream` : `${policy.homeRegion}-stream`;
  return writeToStream(targetStream, evt);
}
```

